      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Galvanic Corrosion Prevention Tips\n\n1. **Avoid dissimilar metals**: Use metals close together in the galvanic series\n2. **Isolate metals**: Use non-conductive materials between different metals\n3. **Use cathodic protection**: For important structures, use sacrificial anodes or impressed current systems\n4. **Apply coatings**: Paint or other protective coatings can reduce galvanic effects\n5. **Control electrolyte**: Reduce salinity and increase pH when possible\n6. **Consider surface area**: Minimize the cathode/anode area ratio to reduce current flow"
